/* The camera permission sheet. Shown by iOS under "Own Hub would like to
   access the camera", at the moment she is deciding whether to photograph her
   national ID card. It names what is taken and what happens to it, because
   "to verify your identity" answers neither.

   Must stay in step with NSCameraUsageDescription in Info.plist and with
   ar.lproj/InfoPlist.strings. There is no photo-library key here, in either
   locale, because this app never asks for the library. */
"NSMotionUsageDescription" = "Own Hub uses your phone's motion only to tilt a few illustrations gently. Nothing is recorded or sent.";
"NSCameraUsageDescription" = "Own Hub uses the camera to photograph both sides of your ID card and take one selfie, so we can check that you are a woman. Nothing is uploaded until you tap send. The photographs are read in memory and never stored.";
